@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Managing Microservices with Docker Compose";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "Docker";
    ViewData["ActivePage"] = "ComposeMicroservices";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">
        Docker Compose makes it easy to manage multiple containers for a microservices application.
        With a single configuration file, you can define services, networks, and volumes, and spin them up in one command.
    </p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Section: What is Docker Compose -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What is Docker Compose?</h2>
        <p>
            Docker Compose is a tool for defining and running multi-container Docker applications using a YAML file.
            It helps orchestrate containers for different microservices, databases, and external dependencies.
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Writing docker-compose.yml -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Writing a docker-compose.yml File</h3>
        <p>Here's an example <code>docker-compose.yml</code> for two microservices:</p>

        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>version: '3.8'

services:
  user-service:
    build: ./user-service
    ports:
      - "5000:5000"

  order-service:
    build: ./order-service
    ports:
      - "5001:5001"</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-3">Each service has its own Dockerfile inside its directory. Docker Compose will build and run them together.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Running Docker Compose -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Running Multiple Containers</h3>
        <p>To build and run all services defined in <code>docker-compose.yml</code>:</p>

        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker-compose up -d</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>

        <p>View running services:</p>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>docker-compose ps</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Docker Compose Tips -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Tips & Best Practices</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Use relative paths for local Dockerfile contexts</li>
            <li>Define environment variables in a <code>.env</code> file</li>
            <li>Use named volumes to persist database or cache data</li>
            <li>Define networks explicitly for better control over communication</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Section: Example Folder Structure -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Example Folder Structure</h3>
        <div class="code-snippet bg-light p-3 rounded position-relative">
            <pre class="mb-0"><code>microservices-app/
├── docker-compose.yml
├── user-service/
│   ├── Dockerfile
│   └── server.js
├── order-service/
│   ├── Dockerfile
│   └── server.js</code></pre>
            <button class="btn btn-outline-secondary copy-btn position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-2">Copy</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Summary -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <p>
            Docker Compose simplifies the orchestration of microservices by allowing developers to define and manage services in a single file.
            In the next section, we’ll explore how these services communicate with one another.
        </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Navigation Buttons -->
    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("DockerizedMicroservices", "Docker")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">
            &larr; Previous: Creating Dockerized Microservices
        </a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("MicroservicesCommunication", "Docker")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">
            Next: Microservices Communication in Docker &rarr;
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- Copy Script -->
<script>
    document.querySelectorAll('.copy-btn').forEach(btn => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
            const codeText = this.parentElement.querySelector('code')?.innerText;
            if (codeText) {
                navigator.clipboard.writeText(codeText).then(() => {
                    alert('Code copied to clipboard!');
                });
            }
        });
    });
</script>
